Rouh on Linux: one command. It checks this server, installs what is missing, and starts Rouh.

Checking this server
  ✓ Debian GNU/Linux 12 (bookworm), x86_64
  ✓ 4 processor cores
  ✓ 10 GB of memory
  ! 55 GB of free disk: Rouh runs, and 64 GB are recommended
  ! Python 3.11.2: Rouh's updater needs 3.12, so it gets a checked copy of its own
  ✓ Port 8420 is free (Rouh's page, on this machine only)
  ✓ Reaches rouh.land, ghcr.io and github.com

What happens now
  · Install: git (with sudo)
  · Install Docker, from Docker's own packages (get.docker.com), with sudo
  · Get Python 3.12.16 for Rouh's updater, into ~/.local/share/rouh/python
  · Get Rouh's updater (rouh-core) into /home/rouh/rouh-core, at the commit rouh.land signed
  · Install the rouh command, and turn on the nightly update (03:00 to 05:00, after a backup)
  · Download and start Rouh: about 2 GB, about 5 minutes
  Nothing of Rouh's listens beyond this machine. Uninstall any time: rouh uninstall

